            "pageCount": 2,
            "processed": true,
            "summary": "This document is a Combined Adverse Event/Product Complaint Report concerning a 29-year-old male patient who experienced skin inflammation and blistering at the site of application after using Cortivex Cream. The cream was applied topically twice daily from July 20 to July 21, 2026. The onset of reactions occurred within hours of the first application, and the issues were still ongoing at the time of reporting. \n\nThe reporter of this incident is T. Tomlin, a pharmacist based in the USA, who did not note any relevant medical history for the patient. Additionally, the report raises a product defect concern, indicating that there was visible discoloration and an unusual odor in the cream from batch/lot number B4471. No photographs were provided with the report. \n\nGiven that this document addresses both an adverse event and a potential quality issue with a product, it is highly relevant for patient safety and quality complaint reviews. The combination of the patient's reaction and the reported defect raises significant concerns that could affect other users of the product.",
